<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine President Fidel Ramos signs tax law.</title>
<headline>Philippine President Fidel Ramos signs tax law.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine President Fidel Ramos signed an important tax law on Friday, scrapping the ad valorem system on beer and cigarettes and replacing it with specific tax.</p>
<p>The new tax law is expected to raise 6.0 to 6.5 billion in additional yearly revenues.</p>
<p>The administration of President Ramos had been pushing for the law to ensure the sustainability of government revenues over the long term and wean away the government's dependence on foreign loans.</p>
<p>The new tax system, which is computed based on volume, is expected to plug the loopholes which enabled tax evasion.</p>
<p>The old ad valorem tax system was based on the value of the product.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
